# systemd-tmpfiles entries for ZoneMinder.
#
# Directories here are created by systemd-tmpfiles-setup.service at boot, and
# those with an age field are cleaned by systemd-tmpfiles-clean.timer, which
# runs daily.

# Runtime directories. D rather than d: these are emptied at boot, because
# nothing in them is meant to outlive the daemons that wrote it.
D @ZM_RUNDIR@ 0755 @WEB_USER@ @WEB_GROUP@
D @ZM_TMPDIR@ 0755 @WEB_USER@ @WEB_GROUP@
D @ZM_SOCKDIR@ 0755 @WEB_USER@ @WEB_GROUP@

# The cache busting directory, aged rather than emptied.
#
# cache_bust() in web/includes/functions.php symlinks every css and js file to
# a name with the source file's mtime in it, so each time a source changes a
# new link appears and the old one is left behind. Nothing has ever removed
# them. The install this was written on had 8346 entries going back to April
# 2020, 1562 of them pointing at files that no longer exist, in a directory
# whose inode had grown to 823KB -- which every lookup in that directory has
# to scan.
#
# Ageing it is safe because the contents are derived, not authoritative: a
# link removed while it is still wanted is recreated by the next page render,
# so the worst case is one missing asset on a page that was already open.
#
# The age is generous on purpose. A symlink's mtime and ctime are fixed when it
# is created, and being served does not refresh them -- traversing a symlink
# does not update its atime either -- so an age deletes entries whether or not
# they are in use, rather than only the unused ones. 30d keeps about a month of
# source versions and costs a few recreated symlinks a month, where 1d would
# churn the whole set daily for no extra benefit.
d @ZM_CACHEDIR@ 0755 @WEB_USER@ @WEB_GROUP@ 30d
